er task (in this paper, we use n=200𝑛200n=200 and k100𝑘100k\\leq 100), count the number of correct samples cn𝑐𝑛c\\leq n which pass unit tests). The HuggingFace code_eval metric implements this same estimator, with the paper cited as its source.\n- **Headline result:** 77.5% with 100 samples (Fig. 1; Table 1).\n- **Authors:** The first author is Mark Chen. Wojciech Zaremba is listed among the authors in the arXiv metadata, and the paper is cited as arXiv:2107.03374 (2021).\n\nSources: arxiv.org/pdf/2107.03374, ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2107.03374, and HuggingFace's code_eval metric page. Only the arXiv PDF and ar5iv are primary; the rest are secondary."],"durationSeconds":6.888247579999999,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01X1YpuWcocBT6WrdZeYwPMz","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
