hi, Eunsol Choi, Daniel S. Weld, and Luke Zettlemoyer. The ACL Anthology lists it at pages 1601–1611 of the 55th Annual Meeting proceedings in Vancouver, and it is also on arXiv as 1705.03551.\n\n- **Dataset size:** The paper describes a reading comprehension dataset of over 650K question-answer-evidence triples. Its question-answer pairs were written by trivia enthusiasts, and the evidence documents were gathered independently.\n- **Key characteristics:** Compared with other large-scale datasets, the authors report more complex compositional questions, more variability between questions and answer-evidence sentences, and more cross-sentence reasoning.\n- **Baselines:** The authors tested a feature-based classifier and a neural network. Their results were 23% and 40% against 80% for humans, which they cite as evidence that the dataset remains a hard testbed.\n- **Resources:** Data and code are available at the project page on the University of Washington site (nlp.cs.washington.edu/triviaqa/).\n\nOne search result, an ar5iv mirror page, contained unrelated text in its excerpt, so I relied on the other sources for the details above.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8a867cf8-27b7-4a02-a79a-db20ed0dcd08","uuid":"d3697aa8-84c5-4eb5-932c-044765b3e14d","timestamp":"2026-10-30T22:15:45.456Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"TriviaQA: A Large Scale Distantly Supervised Challenge Dataset for Reading Comprehension Joshi Choi Weld Zettlemoyer ACL 2017","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01ESczQevJSgA8ZmxMHyxmNv","content":[{"title":"TriviaQA: A Large Scale Distantly Supervised Challenge Dataset for Reading Comprehension","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1705.03551"},{"title":"TriviaQA: A Large Scale Distantly Supervised Challenge Dataset for Reading Comprehension","url":"https://alphaxiv.org/abs/1705.03551"},{"title":"TriviaQA: A Large Scale Distantly Supervised Challen