{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P879MUj6S1koKskTdy2F8k","type":"tool_result","content":"# Reference palette\n\nThis is the **reference instance** of the data-viz method: every parameter the\nmethod needs, filled in with a validated default palette. The rest of the skill\nis system-agnostic - **to target your brand, substitute this file's values** and\nre-run the validator. Nothing else changes.\n\n## How to use these values\n\nEverything below is plain hex. In an HTML chart, **define the slots you use as\nCSS custom properties in a local `<style>` block** at the top of the file, then\nreference them by role throughout - so the light/dark values swap in one place,\nand the chart body is written against roles rather than raw hex:\n\n```css\n.viz-root {\n  color-scheme: light;\n  --surface-1:      #fcfcfb;   /* chart surface */\n  --text-primary:   #0b0b0b;\n  --text-secondary: #52514e;\n  --series-1:       #2a78d6;   /* categorical slot 1 */\n  /* ...only the roles this chart uses */\n}\n@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {\n  :root:where(:not([data-theme=\"light\"])) .viz-root {\n    color-scheme: dark;\n    --surface-1:      #1a1a19;\n    --text-primary:   #f0efec;\n    --text-secondary: #c3c2b7;\n    --series-1:       #3987e5;\n  }\n}\n:root[data-theme=\"dark\"] .viz-root {\n  color-scheme: dark;\n  --surface-1:      #1a1a19;\n  --text-primary:   #f0efec;\n  --text-secondary: #c3c2b7;\n  --series-1:       #3987e5;\n}\n```\n\nDeclare the dark values under both scopes as above - the media query covers\nthe OS setting; the `data-theme` scope covers the viewer's theme toggle,\nwhich must win both ways (the `:not(...)` guard lets a light stamp beat\nOS-dark; `:where()` keeps the media block below the toggle scope).\n\n## Categorical palette\n\nBoth modes are selected. The dark column is the same eight hues stepped for the\ndark surface, not a separate palette:\n\nPalette (light, surface #fcfcfb, categorical): 4 slots\n  [PASS] Lightness band         all 4 inside L 0.43–0.77\n  [PASS] Chroma floor           all 4 >= 0.1\n  [FAIL] CVD separation         worst adjacent #c0446f↔#2e9e6b ΔE 4.9 (deutan) · tritan 28.5\n  [PASS] Normal-vision floor    worst adjacent #2e9e6b↔#d9772a ΔE 22.4 (normal)\n  [PASS] Contrast vs surface    all 4 >= 3:1\n\n  → FAILED — fix the marked checks  (CVD in the 6–8 floor band is legal ONLY with secondary encoding: direct labels, gaps, or texture)\n  scope: categorical palettes only. For a lone status/text color check WCAG text contrast; for a sequential ramp, lightness monotonicity.\n\n/usr/share/texlive/texmf-dist/tex/latex/pgf/frontendlayer/tikz.sty\ngeneral.tex\nmacros.tex\nmath.tex\n23:\\def\\figref#1{figure~\\ref{#1}}\n24:\\def\\Figref#1{Figure~\\ref{#1}}\n25:\\def\\twofigref#1#2{figures \\ref{#1} and \\ref{#2}}\n26:\\def\\quadfigref#1#2#3#4{figures \\ref{#1}, \\ref{#2}, \\ref{#3} and \\ref{#4}}\n29:\\def\\secref#1{section~\\ref{#1}}\n30:\\def\\Secref#1{Section~\\ref{#1}}\n31:\\def\\twosecrefs#1#2{sections \\ref{#1} and \\ref{#2}}\n32:\\def\\secrefs#1#2#3{sections \\ref{#1}, \\ref{#2} and \\ref{#3}}\n46:\\def\\tabref#1{table~\\ref{#1}}\n47:\\def\\Tabref#1{Table~\\ref{#1}}\n63:\\DeclareMathOperator*{\\argmax}{arg\\,max}\n64:\\DeclareMathOperator*{\\argmin}{arg\\,min}\n65:\\DeclareMathOperator{\\sign}{sign}\n66:\\DeclareMathOperator{\\Tr}{Tr}\n205:\\newcommand{\\E}{\\mathbb{E}}\n208:\\newcommand{\\R}{\\mathbb{R}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8a867cf8-27b7-4a02-a79a-db20ed0dcd08","uuid":"3fe88d16-dcce-457c-b5e3-a4d4fee7d093","timestamp":"2026-10-30T22:17:03.259Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Reference palette\n\nThis is the **reference instance** of the data-viz method: every parameter the\nmethod needs, filled in with a validated default palette. The rest of the skill\nis system-agnostic - **to target your brand, substitute this file's values** and\nre-run the validator. Nothing else changes.\n\n## How to use these values\n\nEverything below is plain hex. In an HTML chart, **define the slots you use as\nCSS custom properties in a local `<style>` block** at the top of the file, then\nreference them by role throughout - so the light/dark values swap in one place,\nand the chart body is written against roles rather than raw hex:\n\n```css\n.viz-root {\n  color-scheme: light;\n  --surface-1:      #fcfcfb;   /* chart surface */\n  --text-primary:   #0b0b0b;\n  --text-secondary: #52514e;\n  --series-1:       #2a78d6;   /* categorical slot 1 */\n  /* ...only the roles this chart uses */\n}\n@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {\n  :root:where(:not([data-theme=\"light\"])) .viz-root {\n    color-scheme: dark;\n    --surface-1:      #1a1a19;\n    --text-primary:   #f0efec;\n    --text-secondary: #c3c2b7;\n    --series-1:       #3987e5;\n  }\n}\n:root[data-theme=\"dark\"] .viz-root {\n  color-scheme: dark;\n  --surface-1:      #1a1a19;\n  --text-primary:   #f0efec;\n  --text-secondary: #c3c2b7;\n  --series-1:       #3987e5;\n}\n```\n\nDeclare the dark values under both scopes as above - the media query covers\nthe OS setting; the `data-theme` scope covers the viewer's theme toggle,\nwhich must win both ways (the `:not(...)` guard lets a light stamp beat\nOS-dark; `:where()` keeps the media block below the toggle scope).\n\n## Categorical palette\n\nBoth modes are selected. The dark column is the same eight hues stepped for the\ndark surface, not a separate palette:\n\nPalette (light, surface #fcfcfb, categorical): 4 slots\n  [PASS] Lightness band         all 4 inside L 0.43–0.77\n  [PASS] Chroma floor           all 4 >= 0.1\n  [FAIL] CVD separation         worst adjacent #c0446f↔#2e9e6b ΔE 4.9 (deutan) · tritan 28.5\n  [PASS] Normal-vision floor    worst adjacent #2e9e6b↔#d9772a ΔE 22.4 (normal)\n  [PASS] Contrast vs surface    all 4 >= 3:1\n\n  → FAILED — fix the marked checks  (CVD in the 6–8 floor band is legal ONLY with secondary encoding: direct labels, gaps, or texture)\n  scope: categorical palettes only. For a lone status/text color check WCAG text contrast; for a sequential ramp, lightness monotonicity.\n\n/usr/share/texlive/texmf-dist/tex/latex/pgf/frontendlayer/tikz.sty\ngeneral.tex\nmacros.tex\nmath.tex\n23:\\def\\figref#1{figure~\\ref{#1}}\n24:\\def\\Figref#1{Figure~\\ref{#1}}\n25:\\def\\twofigref#1#2{figures \\ref{#1} and \\ref{#2}}\n26:\\def\\quadfigref#1#2#3#4{figures \\ref{#1}, \\ref{#2}, \\ref{#3} and \\ref{#4}}\n29:\\def\\secref#1{section~\\ref{#1}}\n30:\\def\\Secref#1{Section~\\ref{#1}}\n31:\\def\\twosecrefs#1#2{sections \\ref{#1} and \\ref{#2}}\n32:\\def\\secrefs#1#2#3{sections \\ref{#1}, \\ref{#2} and \\ref{#3}}\n46:\\def\\tabref#1{table~\\ref{#1}}\n47:\\def\\Tabref#1{Table~\\ref{#1}}\n63:\\DeclareMathOperator*{\\argmax}{arg\\,max}\n64:\\DeclareMathOperator*{\\argmin}{arg\\,min}\n65:\\DeclareMathOperator{\\sign}{sign}\n66:\\DeclareMathOperator{\\Tr}{Tr}\n205:\\newcommand{\\E}{\\mathbb{E}}\n208:\\newcommand{\\R}{\\mathbb{R}}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01P879MUj6S1koKskTdy2F8k","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
