{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZCd92hn9VLc9dnbkCjc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The paper is finished and compiles to a 10-page PDF, `paper_draft/main.pdf`, with no LaTeX errors, undefined references or overfull boxes. Its title is *No Universal Temperature: Quality Falls at Model-Specific Cliffs Across Tasks, Sizes, and Families*. I looked over every page after the main compile. The last small fixes, including a slightly enlarged overview figure, compiled cleanly but I did not re-inspect those pages. Nothing is committed.\n\nI recomputed the report's tables and counts from `results/analysis/*.csv`, and they held up except for the points below.\n\n**Where the paper differs from `REPORT.md`:**\n- **Llama-3.1-8B judge drop at T = 1.4:** the data gives 62% (0.6248), not 63%. The nine-model range is therefore 48–62%.\n- **QA \"9/10 worse by 0.7–5.2 points\":** this mixed two groups. All 10 models are lower, 9 of them significantly, by 2.0–5.2 points. The 0.7-point figure is Qwen2.5-14B, which is not significant (p = .217).\n- **Family result:** Gemma sits between the two groups, so the paper says so rather than grouping it with the others. Gemma's gap to Llama (0.118) is about the same as its gaps to Qwen and Mistral (about 0.10).\n- **QA and code family gaps:** the paper adds that these are weaker evidence, because the seed noise floors are larger on those tasks.\n- **Added from the CSVs:**\n  - The largest drop in pass@1 from T = 0.6 to 1.0 is 28%, under the plan's example of 30%.\n  - The best T for pass@4 ranges from 0.4 to 1.4.\n  - Qwen's code useful range does not rise steadily with size.\n  - The Llama ladder crosses versions 3.2 and 3.1.\n- **Falling semantic diversity:** the paper calls the embedding explanation our reading, not a tested result. The report had stated it as fact.\n\n**Citations:** I checked all of them online and took the bibliographic details from those sources.\n- The paper adds TriviaQA and WritingPrompts dataset citations. Both are ACL papers.\n- The Holm 1979 reference is from memory and was not checked online.\n- The Chen et al. entry lists the first ten authors, then \"others\".\n- Related work says plainly that there was no systematic literature search. It also gives Renze & Guven's actual range (nine models, T up to 1.6), because the plan's \"rarely above T=1.0\" doesn't fit that paper.\n\n**Figures:**\n- I redrew the useful-range and story-frontier figures because their labels overlapped, and added a normalized quality figure. The family colors passed the palette check.\n- Those three are generated by `figures/make_figures.py`.\n- A TikZ overview diagram is also new, and the other two figures are the originals.\n\n**Other choices:**\n- The author line is `NeuriCo` as instructed; `.neurico/idea.yaml` doesn't exist anyway.\n- `paper_examples/` holds only a README, so style came from the lab guide.\n- I skipped the skill's optional `paper/OUTLINE.md` because your output structure doesn't include it.\n\n`appendix/` is empty because no appendix was needed.\n\nSources:\n- [Peeperkorn et al.](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.00492)\n- [Renze & Guven, arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.05201)\n- [Renze & Guven, ACL Anthology](https://preview.aclanthology.org/new-sigs/2024.findings-emnlp.432/)\n- [Chen et al.](https://arxiv.org/abs/2107.03374)\n- [Holtzman et al.](https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.09751)\n- [Fan et al.](https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.04833)\n- [Joshi et al.](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1705.03551)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1792,"cache_read_input_tokens":152888,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1792},"output_tokens":782,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8a867cf8-27b7-4a02-a79a-db20ed0dcd08","uuid":"847016dc-586d-4ff0-8a07-a36cb67bc654","timestamp":"2026-10-30T22:21:31.303Z","request_id":"req_011CgZCd8ooRtfNpmrVJhQnu"}
